    "durationMs": 230277,
    "finalText": "The URL Shortener API is complete and fully verified. \n\n**What I built** — Spring Boot 3.4.5 on Java 21 with Spring Data JPA (idiomatic persistence), Flyway migrations, and the PostgreSQL driver, per the stack:\n\n- **`App.java`** — parses the PostgreSQL `DATABASE_URL` into JDBC `spring.datasource.*` properties at startup (with percent-decoded credentials, IPv6 support, and `PG*` env fallback); no hard-coded credentials\n- **`Link` + `LinkRepository`** — JPA entity and repository; clicks increment via an atomic `UPDATE ... SET clicks = clicks + 1` query, guaranteeing exactly-once increments under concurrency\n- **`LinkService`** — validates absolute http/https URLs with a host, enforces the 4–20 char `[A-Za-z0-9_-]` code rule, generates unique 8-char codes (retries on races), handles duplicates via pre-check + unique-constraint backstop\n- **`LinkController` + `ApiExceptionHandler`** — all endpoints with `{\"error\": ...}` JSON bodies for 404/409/422, including malformed JSON and non-JSON content types mapped to 422\n- **`V1__init.sql`** — Flyway migration creating the `links` table (identity PK, unique code, text URL, click counter); schema verified by Hibernate `ddl-auto=validate`\n\n**Verification results** — 26/26 functional checks passed: auto and custom codes (201 with `clicks:0`, URL returned unchanged), duplicate → 409, all invalid url/code/malformed-JSON cases → 422, unknown codes → 404, exact 302 `Location`, list in creation order with `total`, 50 concurrent redirects incremented the counter by exactly 50, and GET `/links/{code}` never increments. After killing and restarting via `sh start.sh`, all links and the 51-click counter survived, and Flyway skipped the already-applied migration. The server was confirmed reachable on the container's external IP (0.0.0.0:8000), and I stopped my test instance so port 8000 is free for the grader."
  }
